        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            Is the result actually random, or can it be influenced?
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              The result is genuinely random. It's calculated using the browser's
              Web Cryptography API (<code>crypto.getRandomValues()</code>) with
              rejection sampling before the spin animation even begins — the
              animation is a visual reveal of an already-decided outcome, so
              click timing can't influence it. For a plain-English explanation,
              see
              <a
                href="https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/is-spin-wheel-truly-random"
                >whether a digital spin wheel is truly random</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            What if the winner can't receive their recognition that day?
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>
              Screenshot the result and carry it forward to the next meeting or
              announcement. The live draw is what matters for transparency — the
              timing of the formal presentation is a separate, secondary step.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">
